Title: 0002-aros-list-and-nprocessors
Repository: skia
Base-Commit: 588b550a4dd8af90dbe71c0554852806bd8f0b21
Requires: 0001-aros-posix-file-memory.patch
Author: aros-skia
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS x86_64 ABIv11 CPU Skia core. Not checked on mainline v1.

Problem:
  ABIv11 pthread.h pulls exec/lists.h (struct List), so Skia's file-scope using List collides. posixc has no _SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN, which SkExecutor uses for the thread pool size.
Solution:
  Qualify SkIDChangeListener::List. On AROS, size the pool with std::thread::hardware_concurrency (1 if that returns 0) instead of sysconf.
Validation:
  AROS x86_64 ABIv11, GCC 13.4.0: SkIDChangeListener.cpp and SkExecutor.cpp
  compile; the examples pass on AROS One (docs/testing.md).
Removal:
  List qualification is permanent while pthread.h pulls exec/lists.h.
  hardware_concurrency stays until posixc defines _SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN.
  Not checked on mainline v1.

diff --git a/src/core/SkExecutor.cpp b/src/core/SkExecutor.cpp
index 4c97f7ffc2..d82a76cabc 100644
--- a/src/core/SkExecutor.cpp
+++ b/src/core/SkExecutor.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@ using namespace skia_private;
         GetNativeSystemInfo(&sysinfo);
         return (int)sysinfo.dwNumberOfProcessors;
     }
+#elif defined(__AROS__)
+    // posixc unistd.h has no _SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN.
+    static int num_cores() {
+        unsigned n = std::thread::hardware_concurrency();
+        return n > 0 ? (int)n : 1;
+    }
 #else
     #include <unistd.h>
     static int num_cores() {
